  "article_notes": "Retrospective laboratory study (Laboklin, Germany), 342 PCR+sequencing-confirmed B. canis dogs, first positive sample, no prior imidocarb/antibiotics/immunosuppressants. No clinical outcome or clinical severity groups are reported (questionnaire outcome data not analysed). The only severity measure is the authors' hematological score (HES), a clinicopathological score built from grades of anaemia, thrombocytopenia, leukopenia, leukocytosis and pancytopenia; extracted as a severity_grade (score) definition. Rows are Spearman correlations with HES (Table 3, HES row) and HES compared between serostatus and travel-history groups. Marker-marker correlations (e.g. CRP vs parasitaemia, antibodies vs parasitaemia) and comparisons of CRP/antibodies/parasitaemia by travel history are not severity and were not extracted. Haematology parameters (PCV, platelets, WBC) are components of HES and their correlations with HES are only in the supplement.",
